{"tool_name":"resistancebank.org","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"resistancebank.org","home":"http://resistancebank.org","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"open-access repository for surveys of antimicrobial resistance in animals.","addition_date":"2021-11-21T15:43:39.371162Z","last_update_date":"2021-11-21T15:45:22.388900Z","tool_type":["Database portal","Web application"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:resistancebank.org","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"nicola.criscuolo@usys.ethz.ch","name":"Nicola G. Criscuolo","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0394-0888","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Cheng Zhao","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3176-0593"},{"name":"Jo\u00e3o Pires","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9738-4423"},{"name":"Thomas P. Van Boeckel","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6556-0952"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Antimicrobial resistance prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3482"}]}],"name":"resistancebank.org","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/S41597-021-00978-9","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2021, The Author(s).Antimicrobial resistance (AMR) is a growing threat to the health of humans and animals that requires global actions. In high-income countries, surveillance systems helped inform policies to curb AMR in animals. In low- and middle-income countries (LMICs), demand for meat is rising, and developing policies against AMR is urgent. However, surveillance of AMR is at best nascent, and the current evidence base to inform policymakers is geographically heterogeneous. We present resistancebank.org, an online platform that centralizes information on AMR in animals from 1,285 surveys from LMICs. Surveys were conducted between 2000 and 2019 and include 22,403 resistance rates for pathogens isolated from chickens, cattle, sheep, and pigs. The platform is built as a shiny application that provides access to individual surveys, country-level reports, and maps of AMR at 10 \u00d7 10 kilometers resolution. The platform is accessed via any internet browser and enables users to upload surveys to strengthen a global database. resistancebank.org aims to be a focal point for sharing AMR data in LMICs and to help international funders prioritize their actions.","authors":[{"name":"Criscuolo N.G."},{"name":"Pires J."},{"name":"Van Boeckel T.P."},{"name":"Zhao C."}],"date":"2021-12-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Scientific Data","title":"resistancebank.org, an open-access repository for surveys of antimicrobial resistance in animals"},"pmcid":"PMC8298417","pmid":"34294731"}],"topic":[{"term":"Biological databases","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3071"},{"term":"Literature and language","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3068"},{"term":"Public health and epidemiology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3305"},{"term":"Zoology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3500"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"resistancebank.org","home":"https://bio.tools/resistancebank.org","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"open-access repository for surveys of antimicrobial resistance in animals.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:resistancebank.org/db/resistancebank.org","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":false,"sourcecode":{"free":null,"interpreted":true,"license":null,"public":true,"readme":false,"repository":{"anonymous":null,"online":null}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":16,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2021"},{"count":1,"year":"2022"},{"count":2,"year":"2023"},{"count":3,"year":"2